OL,3,ANetherlands to return to Eurovision
OL,4,Aafter 2026 boycott
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Netherlands will return to the
OL,7,FEurovision Song Contest next year
OL,8,Fdespite a boycott by the broadcaster
OL,9,Fthat was previously in charge of the
OL,10,Fcountry's participation.
OL,12,FDutch network Avrotros withdrew in 2026
OL,13,Fand said it would also not take part in
OL,14,F2027 because the competition could "no
OL,15,Flonger be considered neutral" given
OL,16,Fdivisions over Israel's involvement and
OL,17,Fthe Gaza war.
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,165,160,200,105,0,100
PN,16402
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F164A1790184254
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ANetherlands to return to Eurovision
OL,4,Aafter 2026 boycott
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe NPO, which oversees public
OL,7,Fbroadcasting in the country, has now
OL,8,Fstepped in, saying the contest will be
OL,9,Faired by broadcasting organisation NOS,
OL,10,Fwhile an independent panel will select
OL,11,Fthe Dutch participant.
OL,13,FJurre Bosman, NPO's director of media,
OL,14,Fsaid: "It is important that, as a
OL,15,Fpublic broadcaster, we remain part of
OL,16,Fthis unifying European event at this
OL,17,Fmoment in particular."
OL,23,APub: 23-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
